<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-gray-700">
  <.header>
    Terms of use
    <:subtitle>A few ground rules for the shared demo.</:subtitle>
  </.header>

  <div class="card space-y-8 p-6 leading-[1.65] sm:p-8">
    <section aria-labelledby="terms-demo">
      <h2 id="terms-demo" class="about-subheading">It's a demo</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Modern Fashion Store is a portfolio project. Nothing is for sale, no orders are shipped,
        and all products, prices and sales are made up. The service comes without any warranty
        and may be offline or reset at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="terms-shared">
      <h2 id="terms-shared" class="about-subheading">The data is shared</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Every visitor uses the same demo account and sees the same catalogue. Don't enter
        personal information, passwords or anything you wouldn't want others to read. Changes
        are removed by the nightly reset at {reset_time(@reset)} ({@reset.timezone}).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="terms-fair">
      <h2 id="terms-fair" class="about-subheading">Fair use</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Please keep content friendly and don't try to overload or break the server. Requests are
        rate-limited, and the catalogue holds at most {@max_products} products.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="terms-photos">
      <h2 id="terms-photos" class="about-subheading">Photos and code</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Product photos come from Pexels (Pexels license), StockSnap and the WordPress photo directory (both CC0).
      </p>
      <p :if={@repository} class="mt-2">
        The source code is public: <.link href={@repository} class="about-link">view it on GitHub</.link>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
